{"shortDescription":"The New Zealand dollar slipped to $0.558 on Wednesday, approaching its lowest level since November 2025, as weak jobs data reduced expectations of further rate hikes by the Reserve Bank.The unemployment rate rose to 5.7% in the third quarter from 5.6% in the previous quarter and beat forecasts of 5…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The New Zealand dollar slipped to $0.558 on Wednesday, approaching its lowest level since November 2025, as weak jobs data reduced expectations of further rate hikes by the Reserve Bank."]},{"type":"p","children":["The unemployment rate rose to 5.7% in the third quarter from 5.6% in the previous quarter and beat forecasts of 5.5%."]},{"type":"p","children":["This marked the highest level in eleven years."]},{"type":"p","children":["Employment also fell 0.1% over the quarter, against expectations of a 0.4% increase."]},{"type":"p","children":["The figures suggest continued slack in the labor market and highlight the fragility of the economic recovery, as elevated oil prices and uncertainty ahead of the November 7 election weigh on business confidence and hiring activity."]},{"type":"p","children":["The deterioration in labor-market conditions casts doubt on the need for further monetary tightening."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets have lowered the probability of a December rate hike to below 50%, down from around 75% the previous day."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:597827:0","title":"New Zealand Dollar Slips After Weak Jobs Report","published":1793752682,"urgency":2,"permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:NZDUSD","currency-logoid":"country/US","base-currency-logoid":"country/NZ","logo":{"style":"pair","logoid":"country/NZ","logoid2":"country/US"}},{"symbol":"FTMO_OANDA:NZDUSD.SIM","currency-logoid":"country/U